  "construction": "Construction I of arXiv:2610.19451 (Nourozi, Smarandache, Mitchell, 'High-Girth QLDPC Codes from Circulant and Affine Permutation Matrices'), Eqs. (8)-(9), at N=37: a fixed 2x6 circulant pattern H_X = [[I]*6; [C_a0..C_a5]], H_Z = [[C_b0..C_b5]; [C_c0..C_c5]] with shift lists a = (0,1,3,8,12,18), b = (0,-5,-5,0,12,12), c = (0,0,2,8,2,8) reduced mod N and C_s the NxN cyclic shift P_{t->t+s}. Theorem 1: CSS by even multiplicity of -b,-c,a-b,a-c; ranks 2N-1 per side (connected incidence graphs); Tanner girth 12 for N=31 and every N >= 37; distance exactly 6, witnessed by the uniform weight-6 logical of their Eq. (12). The attached X-side witness is that operator mirrored through the incidence-graph isomorphism pi = (3,2,1,0,5,4) of the rank proof. Parameters [[6N,2N+2,6]] are Table I of the paper; reproduced here and self-checked against the paper's Example 2 before submission.",
